{
    "background_story": "Jaxson was a renowned children's book author known for his whimsical tales of adventure and fantasy. However, his most notable work was not his original stories, but rather his sanitized adaptations of classic literature. Jaxson believed that the original works of great authors like Shakespeare and Dickens were too racy for young minds, so he took it upon himself to 'clean them up'. His versions of the classics, though lacking in some of the original's nuance and complexity, became incredibly popular among parents and educators. Jaxson's bowdlerized editions were hailed as a way to introduce children to the world of literature without exposing them to 'objectionable' content. While some critics accused him of watering down the originals, Jaxson remained committed to his mission of making great literature accessible to all ages.",
